Now I see the feed logic at bt_monitor.cpp:1042-1069:

```cpp
// Fresh Observation: 
// 1. valid RSSI (!=0 and > -1000)
// 2. AND reading differs from last time (physical fluctuation = real RF)
// only then feedFreshRssi advances baseline; unchanged reading strictly goes to registerDeviceSnapshot
if (info.rssiDbm != 0 && info.rssiDbm > -1000 && info.rssiDbm != prevRssiForFreshCheck) {
    auto deg_ev = tracker_->feedFreshRssi(k, info.rssiDbm, wall_ms, mono_ns);
    ...
} else {
    tracker_->registerDeviceSnapshot(k, wall_ms, mono_ns);
}
```

So for the degraded streak to advance, each poll must produce a **different** RSSI value from the previous one. Looking at the journal data:

```
03:08:04  iQOO -81  vivo -82
03:08:22  iQOO -71  vivo -82
03:08:40  iQOO -74  vivo -82
03:08:59  iQOO -77  vivo -82
